// AddDomain calls add_domain: POST
// /v1/capabilities/infrastructures/:infrastructure_id/domains.
//
// Attach a custom domain to an infrastructure and start its HTTPS certificate.
//
// DNS FIRST. Call list_domains for the infrastructure's `load_balancer_ip` (or,
// for an l7 domain, its `application_address`), have the USER create a record
// for the domain pointing at it, and wait for it to resolve. This call verifies
// DNS before it writes anything and refuses the domain outright if the record
// is missing or points somewhere else — that refusal is not a platform fault,
// it is the work the user still has to do at their registrar. You cannot do it
// for them.
//
