// ApproveChartApplication calls approve_chart_application: POST
// /v1/capabilities/applications/:application_id/chart-approvals.
//
// Approve what an operator chart's waiting release asks for across the cluster,
// so it installs.
//
// People only, an admin of the instance. An operator chart (Strimzi, a database
// operator) asks for powers across the whole cluster: its own resource types,
// roles beyond its namespace, admission webhooks. Its release waits at
// awaiting_approval, its summary's `powers` saying each in words with what to
// read twice (`risks`), until an admin approves them; the approval covers
// exactly those grants, what runs with them (`runs`: every pod of the chart,
// its images, commands and environment, the data of the ConfigMaps and Secrets
// it reads but what the chart generated, and as whom), the objects its operator
// acts on (`objects`, each whole) and every risk said, so a later version
// asking for the same or less installs without asking, and one asking for more,
// or running other code with them, waits again. A chart that holds nothing
// across the cluster waits too when its objects are of a resource type another
// chart application brings: `objects` names that application, whose operator
// acts on them with its powers. Once an application has been approved, every
// later version waits for an admin unless an approval covers it — what it runs
// and keeps (`config`), its objects — one holding nothing across the cluster
// too (`approved_before`: this application has been approved before: every
// version of it is approved); the first approval approves what earlier,
// unapproved versions left in its namespace as it stands (`kept`, the runs
// marked `kept` and `kept_disks`, by name, never a value), so the upgrade after
// it asks once more; and approving one over what such a version left running
// (`quiesce`) stops it — its KEDA autoscalers paused first — and replaces the
// namespace's service accounts, before anything of the approved version is
// applied, starting again once it is installed what that version makes; what
// another operator makes there from its own objects (a CloudNativePG Cluster, a
// Prometheus) is left running, and refused where it runs as an account the
// chart empowers. A version of an approved application making nothing else is
// approved as a whole (`whole`), so the same version rendered again is covered.
// `fingerprint` is the powers' the admin read: a release waiting with others is
// refused, to be read again.
//
// It needs the infrastructure:provision permission, changes state and is not
// offered to agents or service accounts (surfaces: console, cli).
func (c *Client) ApproveChartApplication(ctx context.Context, p ApproveChartApplicationParams) (json.RawMessage, error) {
	return c.invoke(ctx, "approve_chart_application", p.args())
}

