// DESTRUCTIVE AND FINAL.
//
// Starts DestroyInfrastructureWorkflow, which is provisioning run backwards:
// every application on the cluster is deleted, the installed apps are
// uninstalled (Postgres and Redis pools, then the platform's own gateway,
// monitoring and CI/CD in reverse install order), then Terraform destroys the
// GKE cluster and its node pools, then the VPC, Cloud NAT, firewall rules and,
// for a zero-trust infrastructure, its NCC spoke — and the instance's hub with
// it when no other spoke is left — and finally the state bucket. The
// infrastructure record is deleted LAST — it is what makes a partial teardown
// recoverable, so it survives until nothing is left for it to name. Sequential
// and up to three hours; it returns as soon as the workflow starts. Poll
// get_infrastructure_status.
