// DetectRepository calls detect_repository: GET /v1/capabilities/github/detect.
//
// Inspect a repository and report what can be deployed from it: declared
// services, monorepo layout, languages, ports and Dockerfiles.
//
// CALL THIS BEFORE create_application, every time. It is the only way to see
// what the repository actually declares, and creating an application against a
// wrong picture of it is not cheap to undo — the application name and namespace
// are immutable.
//
// What comes back, in order of authority:
//
// 0. `applications` — every application the manifest declares: `{name,
// namespace, services}`. One file can declare SEVERAL (a monorepo whose
// services all build from the repository root cannot give a second application
// a manifest of its own), and then `multiple_applications` is true and the flat
// `application`, `namespace` and `declared_services` fields are ABSENT —
// deliberately, because there is no single answer and returning one of two
// silently is worse than returning none. create_application's `name` must be
// one of these section keys; it is refused, with the list, when it is not. With
// one application the flat fields are present as before.
// 1. `declared_services` — the root inframan.yaml's services: map, with each
// service's type, path and port. This is AUTHORITATIVE: CI resolves every
// service against it on each push. When it is present, it is the answer, even
// where the directory layout suggests otherwise — one build context can fan out
// into several services (a web process and a worker sharing an image is the
// usual case), and no amount of directory inspection can see that.
// 2. `is_monorepo` and `monorepo_services` — the fallback when there is no
// inframan.yaml: subdirectories that look like separate build contexts.
// 3. `language`, `buildpack`, `has_dockerfile` — a single-service repository.
//
// `inframan_yaml_error` means the file exists and is INVALID. Do not fall back
// to the heuristics and do not create the application: report the error, fix
// the yaml, push, and detect again. create_application refuses it too, and
// later.
//
// `application` and `namespace` are what the yaml declares. They must match the
// application you create byte for byte — CI validates them on every push and
// fails the release on drift.
//
// It needs the settings:read permission, changes nothing and is offered to
// agents and service accounts (surfaces: console, cli, agent).
func (c *Client) DetectRepository(ctx context.Context, p DetectRepositoryParams) (json.RawMessage, error) {
	return c.invoke(ctx, "detect_repository", p.args())
}

