// the answer. Of an on-demand agent it also gives `triggers`, as list_agents
// does, a trigger's `phrase` among them (one phrase is one agent's in the
// instance: a release that gives another agent a phrase this one holds is
// refused, AGENT_TRIGGER_PHRASE_TAKEN); `webhook` (whether a URL has been made
// and when, with the URL's token left out: the URL is shown once, to the person
// who makes it in the console); `recent_runs`, its five newest; and `can_run`
