// `tier`: several named installs of one app can live on one infrastructure, and
// the name is how they are told apart and how services address them. Only
// `basic` tier is available today; a future tier promising replication or
// failover will be accepted only on a prod (regional) infrastructure, because a
// zonal cluster cannot honour it. `memory` is optional and Redis-only.
// `persistence` is optional for every add-on — omitted takes the app's default
// (on), Postgres refuses an explicit false, and the choice cannot be changed
// after the install.
